    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nI'd like to set multiple mappings for some things in mini.files (other mini modules may have the same problem),\ncurrently mini.files checks that each mapping is a string, making this impossible.\n\nIt looks like the are eventually to `vim.keymap.set` which accepts a table of mappings here, so I think this is just a matter of changing the type checking to accept a string or table.",
